cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this deposit, please cite the manuscript and (optionally) this software/data release."
type: dataset
title: "Zenodo Deposit accompanying *Mapping Structured Absences in Scientific Papers: An Auditable LLM-Assisted Workflow Demonstrated on Cross-Coupling Chemistry* (UQS methodology, 9-tier audit-trail organisation)"
abstract: >
  Prompts, redacted analysis outputs, classification tables, figures, retrieval logs,
  audit decisions, and reproducibility utilities for the UQS (Unasked Question
  Structuring) methodology applied to a 54-year cartography of the Kumada 1972
  Ni-catalysed cross-coupling chemistry literature. Public version with verbatim
  source-paper quotations redacted (see Tier 8 for redacted outputs). The reviewer version,
  with the full outputs, is the Zenodo record with concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23437447, cited in the paper
  (published with its files restricted to the editor and reviewers until acceptance). Companion to:
  Ono, Yoshioka, Taketsugu, "Mapping Structured Absences in Scientific Papers:
  An Auditable LLM-Assisted Workflow Demonstrated on Cross-Coupling Chemistry,"
  Digital Discovery, 2026 (revised version under review).
